          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.05,
            0.432,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.185
          ],
          "content": "In addition to the number line, we used the token model to understand integers. We used this model to perform addition and subtraction in Grade 6. Let us do a quick recall. We used green ( ) token to represent positive 1 and red ( ) token to represent negative 1, that is –1. Together they make zero, as they cancel each other out."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.194,
            0.317,
            0.215
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Find (+7) – (+18)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.22,
            0.846,
            0.258
          ],
          "content": "To subtract 18 from 7, i.e., (+7) – (+18), we need to remove 18 positives from 7 positives."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.368,
            0.268,
            0.628,
            0.3
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.315,
            0.8,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": "But there are not enough tokens to remove 18 positives! We put in enough zero pairs so that we can remove 18 positives."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.361,
            0.274,
            0.384
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "How many?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.388,
            0.845,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": "We have 7 positives and we need 11 more. So we need to put in 11 zero pairs:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.441,
            0.842,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.434,
            0.476,
            0.842,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.525,
            0.478,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": "We can now remove 18 positives."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.558,
            0.841,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.642,
            0.639,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": "What is left? There are 11 negatives, meaning –11."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.422,
            0.673,
            0.576,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": "So, 7 – 18 = –11."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.701,
            0.846,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": "We had also seen that subtracting a number is the same as adding its additive inverse."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.749,
            0.632,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": "Using tokens, argue out the following statements."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.78,
            0.649,
            0.799
          ],
          "content": "(a) 7 – 18 = 7 + (– 18) (additive inverse of 18 is – 18)"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.74,
            0.904,
            0.79
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_4_image_19.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.805,
            0.649,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": "(b) 4 – (– 12) = 4 + 12 (additive inverse of – 12 is 12)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.843,
            0.827,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": "**Note to the Teacher:** Tokens of different shapes may be used for positive and negative numbers for visually challanged students."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.934,
            0.187,
            0.949
          ],
          "content": "28"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
